shonites.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´Those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, even those that were numbered of them were seven thousand and five hundred.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKThe families of the Gershonites shall pitch behind the tabernacle westward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And the chief of the house of the father of the Gershonites shall be Eliasaph the son of Lael.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÌAnd the charge of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation shall be the tabernacle, and the tent, the covering thereof, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´and the hangings of the court, and the curtain for the door of the court, which is by the tabernacle, and by the altar round about, and the cords of it for all the service thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And of Kohath was the family of the Amramites, and the family of the Izeharites, and the family of the Hebronites, and the family of the Uzzielites: these are the families of the Kohathites.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†In the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were eight thousand and six hundred, keeping the charge of the sanctuary.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWThe families of the sons of Kohath shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle southward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd the chief of the house of the father of the families of the Kohathites shall be Elizaphan the son of Uzziel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾And their charge shall be the ark, and the table, and the candlestick, and the altars, and the vessels of the sanctuary wherewith they minister, and the hanging, and all the service thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest shall be chief over the chief of the Levites, and have the oversight of them that keep the charge of the sanctuary.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse%¦verses•„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkOf Merari was the family of the Mahlites, and the family of the Mushites: these are the families of Merari.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were six thousand and two hundred.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœAnd the chief of the house of the father of the families of Merari was Zuriel the son of Abihail: these shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle northward.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàAnd under the custody and charge of the sons of Merari shall be the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and the sockets thereof, and all the vessels thereof, and all that serveth thereto,¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]and the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords.¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse'¦verses’„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ$But those that encamp before the tabernacle toward the east, even before the tabernacle of the congregation eastward, shall be Moses, and Aaron and his sons, keeping the charge of the sanctuary for the charge of the children of Israel; and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉAll that were numbered of the Levites, which Moses and Aaron numbered at the commandment of the LORD, throughout their families, all the males from